<comment datatype='string'>The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-12264&quot;&gt;paaF&lt;/a&gt; gene of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-198931&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Pseudomonas&lt;/i&gt; sp. &lt;i&gt;Y2&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was cloned and expressed in &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-562&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and the recombinant protein was purified to homogeneity [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20660314&quot;&gt;Teufel10&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
The purified protein catalyzed the reversible conversion of enzymatically produced &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=TRANS-23-DEHYDROADIPYL-COA&quot;&gt;(2&lt;i&gt;E&lt;/i&gt;)-5-carboxy-2-pentenoyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt; into &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=3-HYDROXYADIPYL-COA&quot;&gt;(3S)-hydroxyadipyl-CoA&lt;/a&gt;, as evidenced by mass spectrometry [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20660314&quot;&gt;Teufel10&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
